component SigilComparisonScope {
  goal {
    Focus native Design and Implementation comparison on explicit source membership
    so callers do not need duplicate scope assembly.
  }

  interface {
    ScopeInput {
      Accept a versioned scope containing ordered workspace-relative Design root
      paths and the existing language-neutral Implementation selection. Design roots
      name authored Sigil files in the validated frontend bundle. Reject unknown
      fields, duplicate roots, missing roots, paths outside the workspace, and
      accidental empty selection. Intentional emptiness is explicit for each side and
      visible in the result. Without an explicit scope, retain full frontend Design
      membership and ordinary Implementation selection. Reject conflicting selection
      inputs.
    }

    FocusOrder {
      Preserve the caller's explicit root order as focus priority. Do not sort it
      away during normalization or replace it with filesystem discovery order. Return
      that order from scoped commands so the frontend and caller can see what to
      address first and next without a temporary priority table. Report dependency
      additions deterministically after the requested roots, retaining their
      inclusion reasons without displacing explicit priorities. Identify requested
      order separately from unordered effective membership. Reprioritization changes
      order identity, not unchanged semantic bindings. Order guides caller priority;
      sigilc does not schedule interpretation or infer that an earlier entry has been
      completed.
    }

    DesignMembership {
      Resolve Design roots through frontend imports and structural ownership to a
      closed set of physical files. Include transitive import targets and owner
      declarations required by selected Tags and Facets. Terminate cycles with a
      visited set. Preserve every authored unit in each included file with its
      physical source and canonical owner. Report requested roots separately from
      files included by dependency closure. Included dependency files participate in
      Design compilation and catalog construction, rather than supplying hidden
      comparison assumptions. Do not silently drop unresolved references or errors.
      When unresolved imports require conservative full-bundle membership, report
      that widening. Preserve applicable configuration, glossary context and global
      diagnostics. Do not infer source membership from temporary prose or caller
      metadata.
    }

    ScopedComparison {
      Expose scope inspection without requiring reconstructed projections or a
      current catalog. Return current input identities and retained frontend
      diagnostics; inspection success is not a completed semantic gate. Use the same
      resolved scope for freshness inspection, preparation, ingestion, Design
      compilation, catalog export and Implementation comparison. Require per-source
      operations to target a member of their selected side. Report deterministic
      requested and effective membership and its fingerprint alongside current input
      identities and the ordinary native named states. Keep excluded cached objects
      reusable. Distinguish outside-scope objects from deleted sources; neither
      contributes assertions to the selected world.
    }
  }

  constraints {

    StructuralScope {
      Use schema 2 exact selections and explicit owner files. _module.sigil is
      ordinary source with no re-export or directory-import closure. Preserve all
      Facet references, links, contract roles, exact ranges and selected Tag origins;
      imports alone do not prove runtime or semantic dependence.
    }
    SemanticIdentity {
      Scope membership affects assembled worlds and reports. A scope name, filename
      or external requirement ID is not a per-source semantic input. Reuse a
      projection when its existing complete semantic binding is unchanged. A changed
      effective Design identity catalog still invalidates Implementation projections
      under the existing full-catalog binding policy. Scoping never gives
      Implementation interpreters Design prose or relationships; their inputs remain
      captured source, fixed ontology and identity catalog.
    }
  }

  cases {
    DependencyClosure {
      Selecting a file that imports another includes both and reports why the second
      file is present. Import cycles terminate. Selecting consumer Tag use preserves
      its Facet owner and includes the selected provider declaration with complete
      interpretation context. An unrelated excluded file contributes no assertions or
      obligations. An unresolved import cannot manufacture a smaller successful
      world.
    }

    ScopeChanges {
      Reordering the same roots changes reported focus order and its identity, while
      preserving membership identity. Adding a source changes world membership
      without invalidating unchanged per-source inputs. Removing a file from scope
      does not delete it or its cached projection. Narrowing Design enough to change
      catalog identity invalidates dependent Implementation projections instead of
      reusing a previous comparison.
    }

    ObservedPriority {
      Preserve caller-defined priority in native scope output so callers can address
      selected roots in the reported order without maintaining a second
      focus-priority table. Selecting roots A then B reports A first. Reprioritizing
      B then A reports B first without invalidating otherwise identical per-source
      projections. Repeated runs preserve order even when frontend or filesystem
      enumeration changes. The caller still establishes which interpretation is
      complete.

      Focus order is a priority and reporting order, not a demand to serialize
      independent reconstructions. External callers may prepare independent sources
      concurrently while native publication remains authoritative.
    }

    ScopeLimits {
      A typo in a root fails instead of producing an empty green result. A successful
      focused comparison is not reported as complete-refactor convergence. Gate exits
      retain their subcommand-specific named states.
    }
  }
}
